      "role": "user",
      "content": "i get that, but we don't have time for full focus groups right now. we need to make some quick decisions on the design direction. \n\nbe real with me, if we use a super high-end, sleek, 'premium' fintech look—you know, very dark mode, high-contrast, Apple-style—is that going to work everywhere? or is that kind of look going to feel too 'western/elite' for the Nigerian or UAE markets, or maybe even 'too cold' for the Japanese market? i'm trying to understand if certain design languages are inherently tied to specific levels of wealth or social status in these regions.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
