      "content": "The design direction you're considering, while sleek and premium, might not be perceived as accessible or inclusive in non-Western markets. Dark modes and high-contrast aesthetics can be stunning in a Western context, but may be perceived as cold, elitist, or even lazy design in other regions.\n\nStudies have shown that in some African and Middle Eastern societies, high contrast and minimalism can be misinterpreted as a lack of attention to detail, while in some Asian cultures, minimalism is actually highly valued.\n\nFor Nigeria and UAE, a more simplified and bright color palette with bold typography might be more fitting, as it can convey a sense of friendliness and approachability. In Japan, you might focus on a more subtle balance of positive and negative space to convey nuance and strategy.",
